---
/**
 * Indoors — museums, science centers and libraries.
 *
 * The section exists because of the weather, not because of the institutions.
 * Nobody wakes up wanting a decorative arts collection; they wake up to rain
 * on day three of a beach week with two kids in a rental. So the page is
 * organized around "what's open today and does it cost anything", and the H1
 * says the weather part out loud.
 *
 * Hours lead every card. A park is open; these are shut two or three days a
 * week, and two of them are shut for building work right now. The failure mode
 * is a locked door at the end of an hour's drive up Route 1.
 *
 * Grouped by county, like every other section here. Someone in Lewes is not
 * driving to Wilmington for an afternoon, and a flat alphabetical list would
 * pretend otherwise.
 */
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import NearMe from "../../components/NearMe.astro";
import FlagIcon from "../../components/FlagIcon.astro";
import CardPhoto from "../../components/CardPhoto.astro";
import Tag from "../../components/Tag.astro";
import CardShare from "../../components/CardShare.astro";
import Filters from "../../components/Filters.astro";
import CardGallery from "../../components/CardGallery.astro";

import indoorData from "../../data/indoor.json";
import { COUNTY_ORDER, completeness, hoursAnswer, isIndoors, present, type IndoorPlace } from "../../lib/indoor";
import { isPublishable, robotsFor } from "../../lib/verification";
import { byPhotoThen } from "../../lib/order";

const places = (indoorData as unknown as IndoorPlace[]).filter(isIndoors);
const live = places.filter(isPublishable);
const gate = {
  verifiedDate: null,
  verifiedSource: null,
  sources: live.length ? [{ label: "x", url: "x" }] : null,
  sourcedOn: live.length ? "2026-08-04" : null,
};

const free = places.filter((p) => p.admission.free === true).length;
const unknownAdmission = places.filter((p) => p.admission.amount === null && p.admission.free !== true).length;
const shut = places.filter((p) => p.hours.lines === null).length;

const ranked = byPhotoThen(places, (a, b) => completeness(b).known - completeness(a).known);
/* Filters derived from the records, so a chip can never be empty. */
const tagCounts = new Map<string, { key: string; label: string; count: number }>();
for (const r of places) {
  for (const t of present(r)) {
    const e = tagCounts.get(t.key) ?? { key: t.key, label: t.label, count: 0 };
    e.count++;
    tagCounts.set(t.key, e);
  }
}
const filterTags = [...tagCounts.values()].sort((a, b) => b.count - a.count || a.label.localeCompare(b.label));

const byCounty = COUNTY_ORDER.map((county) => ({
  county,
  places: ranked.filter((p) => p.county === county),
})).filter((g) => g.places.length > 0);
---

<Layout
  title="Delaware museums and libraries — hours and admission"
  description="Delaware museums, science centers and libraries by county: opening hours, what admission costs, what's inside. Where to take the kids when it rains at the beach."
  robots={robotsFor(gate)}
>
  <div class="wrap pt-11 pb-6">
    <p class="label m-0">Indoors</p>
    <h1 class="text-[2.2rem] sm:text-[2.9rem] mt-3.5 mb-0 max-w-[15ch] text-marsh">
      When it rains
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 mb-0 text-[1.15rem] leading-[1.5] max-w-[54ch]">
      Museums, natural history, art and fifteen library branches, sorted by
      county. Everywhere here is warm, dry and indoors. The rest of the site
      covers <a href="/parks/">the days you can get outside</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap pb-4">
    <Filters tags={filterTags} noun="places" class="breakout">

      <NearMe noun="places" flat />

    </Filters>
  </div>

  {
    byCounty.map(({ county, places: group }) => (
      <div class="wrap pb-8" data-filter-group>
        <h2 class="label m-0 pb-3">{county} County</h2>
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 breakout">
      {
        group.map((place) => {
          const { known, total } = completeness(place);
          const hrs = hoursAnswer(place.hours);
          const has = present(place);
          return (
            <article data-reveal
                data-lat={place.coords?.lat}
                data-lon={place.coords?.lon} data-tags={has.map((t) => t.key).join(" ")} class="sign sign-action relative group overflow-hidden">
              <a href={`/indoors/${place.slug}/`} class="absolute inset-0 z-10 no-underline">
                <span class="sr-only">{place.name}</span>
              </a>
              <CardShare path={`/indoors/${place.slug}/`} title={place.name} />

              {place.photos?.length && <CardGallery photos={place.photos} />}

              <div class="p-4 sm:p-5">
                <header class="flex items-start justify-between pr-12 gap-3">
                  <div>
                    <h2 class="font-display text-[1.12rem] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] m-0 text-marsh underline decoration-ochre decoration-2 underline-offset-[0.16em] group-hover:decoration-marsh">
                      {place.name}
                    </h2>
                    <p class="stamp text-ink-soft mt-1 mb-0">{place.kind} · {place.town}</p>
                  </div>
                  <span class="stamp text-ink-soft shrink-0">{known}/{total}</span>
                </header>

                {/* Hours first, always, and visually separated. */}
                <div class="mt-3.5 border-y-2 border-marsh py-2.5">
                  <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
                    <span class="label">Open</span>
                    <span
                      class={`text-[0.9rem] text-right leading-snug ${
                        hrs.state === "unknown" ? "text-ink-soft italic" : "text-ink font-medium"
                      }`}
                    >
                      {hrs.text}
                    </span>
                  </div>
                  {place.hours.season && (
                    <p class="stamp text-flag-red-bearing mt-1.5 mb-0 text-right">{place.hours.season}</p>
                  )}
                </div>

                <p class="mt-3 mb-0 text-[0.9rem] leading-[1.55]">{place.blurb}</p>

                {has.length > 0 && (
                  <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 mt-3.5 flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
                    {has.map((f) => (
                      <Tag icon={f.key as any} label={f.label} emphasis={f.emphasis} />
                    ))}
                  </ul>
                )}

                {place.warnings.length > 0 && (
                  <p class="mt-3 mb-0 text-[0.85rem] leading-snug text-ink-soft flex gap-1.5">
                    <FlagIcon icon="alert" class="w-[1em] h-[1em] mt-1 shrink-0 text-flag-red" />
                    <span>{place.warnings[0]}</span>
                  </p>
                )}

                <p class="stamp text-ink-soft mt-3.5 mb-0 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
                  <span>{place.operator}</span>
                  <span class="text-ochre-deep group-hover:translate-x-0.5 transition-transform duration-100">→</span>
                </p>
              </div>
            </article>
          );
        })
      }
        </div>
      </div>
    ))
  }

  <div class="wrap prose-field pb-2">
    <h2>Check the hours before you drive</h2>
    <p class="max-w-[58ch]">
      This is the one section where turning up unannounced doesn't work. The
      Delaware Art Museum and the Biggs are shut Monday and Tuesday. The Old
      State House is shut Sunday through Tuesday. Hagley closes Wednesdays.
      Zwaanendael is shut Sunday and Monday, which is half of a beach weekend.
    </p>

    <p class="max-w-[58ch]">
      Two are shut for building work right now and still show as open on maps:
      the Johnson Victrola Museum until autumn, and the Newark Free Library for
      a construction project. Hagley's powder yard closes 24 August to 4
      September, and admission goes half price while it does.
    </p>

    <p class="max-w-[58ch]">
      So hours sit at the top of every card and every page here, and where I
      don't know them it says so instead of implying you're welcome.
    </p>

    <div class="sign breakout my-6 px-4 sm:px-5 py-4">
      <p class="label m-0">Where this dataset stands</p>
      <dl class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mt-3 mb-0">
        {
          [
            { n: places.length, label: "places listed" },
            { n: free, label: "free to walk into" },
            { n: unknownAdmission, label: "price not published" },
            { n: shut, label: "hours not published" },
          ].map((s) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="font-display text-[2rem] font-semibold text-marsh leading-none">{s.n}</dt>
              <dd class="m-0 mt-1 stamp text-ink-soft">{s.label}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-3.5 mb-0 text-[0.9rem] leading-snug text-ink-soft max-w-[56ch]">
        Every free one here is state-run. Winterthur and the Biggs publish no
        admission price on their visit pages at all — that's not an oversight on
        my end, it's genuinely not published, and both are on the call list.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap prose-field pb-4">
    <h2>Why a library is in here</h2>
    <p class="max-w-[58ch]">
      Because on a wet Tuesday it's the most reliable indoor room in the state.
      Free, warm, has a bathroom, and nobody minds how long you stay. Fifteen
      New Castle County branches keep fifteen different timetables, which is a
      nuisance to look up fifteen times, so they're in one table with the
      number to call beside each one.
    </p>
    <p class="max-w-[58ch]">
      All three counties are in now: fifteen New Castle branches, fourteen in
      Sussex including a bookmobile, and four in Kent. What none of them
      publish in one place is opening hours, so every row carries the address
      and the number to ring instead of a timetable I'd have had to invent.
    </p>

    <h2>Related</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/parks/">The 17 state parks</a></li>
      <li><a href="/parks/community/">Community and county parks</a></li>
      <li><a href="/events/">Fairs and events</a></li>
      <li><a href="/dogs/">Dog rules by town</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Layout>
